# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
.idea/

# Codegraph
#  Codegraph generates a .codegraph directory in the root of the project to store its
#  internal data. This directory should be ignored to prevent it from being committed to version control.
.codegraph/

# CodeGraphContext
mcp.json
login-page.png
.playwright-mcp/

# Local dev secrets (JWT signing keys, TLS certs) — never commit
docker/.secrets/
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Exception: the vendored FIDO MDS3 trust anchor (GlobalSign Root CA - R3).
# It is a *public* root certificate — no private key — and it is the pinned
# root of trust for every WebAuthn attestation policy decision, so it has to
# ship in the tree and in the binary (`include_str!`). Its SHA-256 is pinned
# in code and checked at load; see crates/axiam-pki/src/mds/mod.rs.
!crates/axiam-pki/src/mds/fido-mds-root-ca-r3.pem

# Claude Code dev tooling — generated/ephemeral, reprovisioned by
# scripts/bootstrap-dev-tools.sh (GSD installs globally to ~/.claude).
.claude/
.claude-flow/
.mcp.json
CLAUDE.md.pre-ruflo
.swarm/

# GSD research web-fetch cache (transient)
.planning/research/.cache/

# Python tooling artifacts (benchmark/collect scripts)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# X5.2 — conformance-harness working state. `.run/` holds rendered plan
# configs, which carry client private keys; `certs/` holds the throwaway
# client certificates and their unencrypted keys. The committed artifacts are
# the plan TEMPLATES (conformance/plans/) and the rendered REPORTS
# (docs/conformance/), never the credentials in between.
conformance/.run/
conformance/certs/
stories/
